#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""
weblion-clp: the root wrapper the weblion console runs on a CloudPanel server over SSH.

Remote mode (no arguments): the console's agent user may run exactly this script through sudo,
without arguments. A request arrives as one JSON line on stdin, the answer leaves as one JSON
line on stdout (wire protocol v1): exit code 0 with "ok": true, 1 with "ok": false. Any other
exit code means the script itself failed.

Local mode (arguments, root on the server): status, adopt, forget, protect, refresh-usage,
selftest. "weblion-clp --help" lists them.

This script is the security boundary between the console and the server:
- a closed list of operations, every argument checked against a strict pattern;
- commands run as argument lists without a shell and with a fixed environment;
- only sites on the managed list are changed, protected sites and users never;
- real passwords only travel on stdin of chpasswd and the mysql client; clpctl only ever sees
  random throw-away passwords that are replaced right afterwards; every text that leaves the
  script is cleaned of secrets;
- CloudPanel's SQLite database is only read (read-only, short, outside clp-agent's write slot);
- every change is verified by reading CloudPanel's database afterwards, never by exit codes.

Python 3.9 or newer, standard library only.
"""

